-------------------------------------------------------------------
Sat Nov 07 12:00:00 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Run checks, updates and Resolve in a job thread. packagekitd calls
  the backend on its main thread, and during an update every D-Bus call
  to it timed out after 25 seconds: no progress, no Cancel, and other
  clients hung.
- Add pk_backend_cancel. Without it PackageKit answered "Cancel not
  supported by backend". Cancel turns off once zypper has finished and
  transactional-update is closing the snapshot.
- Wait up to 45 seconds for the network before a check. The check at
  login ran before the network was up and failed in under a second.
  A check that still cannot reach the servers says so in one sentence,
  and every failure is written to the journal.
- Check with the zypper options transactional-update uses, so a check
  that passes means the update will too.
- Name the license abort. transactional-update dup does not agree to
  package licenses, so an NVIDIA driver update aborted with exit 4.
  Discover now says which zypper.conf setting fixes it.
- Show the last lines of a long failure log. The first eight were the
  transactional-update banner and the package list, and the reason was
  in "and 21 more". The backend's own messages are no longer cut.
- A missing repomd.xml is reported as a repository that cannot be
  read, not as packages that are still being published.
- Report the System updates row during an update, so pkcon no longer
  prints "There are no updates available" after staging one.
- Progress only moves forward: downloads fill 0-50, installs 50-100.
- Stop reading a command's output five seconds after it exits. A child
  that kept the pipe open could hang the job.
- Keep the update list on a non-forced refresh. Discover refreshes
  before every check, which made the ten-minute cache useless.
- Cache rpm -qa until Packages.db changes. Resolve went from 0.86 to
  0.01 seconds.
- Run the source tests in %check. Drop %systemd_post and
  %systemd_postun for packagekit.service, which this package does not
  own.
- Release 15. The repository already has 0.1.0-14.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 20:01:02 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Make Flathub the Discover application source. With the distro
  catalog gone, the home page stayed on the PackageKit source and
  showed "Unable to load applications".
- Release 14. The repository already has 0.1.0-12.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 09:20:08 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Send the reboot notification when the update is staged, not when a
  later check runs. That check runs after Discover is closed, and the
  popup was appearing then.
- Let the notification expire, and name it AtropOS. It was set to
  never expire under the name Discover, so it stayed up after the
  window closed.
- Give Notify its argument types explicitly. An untyped 0 is an int,
  and plasmashell rejected the call while it was still starting.
- Release 13. The repository already has 0.1.0-12.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 02:48:33 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- While a snapshot is waiting, a check returns no packages and asks
  for a reboot. Discover then shows its reboot page instead of Update
  All. The notification stamp is written only after gdbus exits 0, so
  a failed notification is tried again on the next check.
- Release 12. The repository already has 0.1.0-11.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 02:25:39 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- After an update is staged, Discover shows "System update" with
  "Installed. Reboot to apply." instead of a package named AtropOS
  version staged and an unknown size.
- Notify the user who started the update, once, that it was installed
  and will be applied after reboot.
- Keep the solved update list while a reboot is waiting, so Discover's
  refresh does not drop the download size.
- Release 11. The repository already has 0.1.0-10.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 01:23:50 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- Parse a successful update check from zypper's stdout only. stderr
  is kept for the failure text, so a warning does not make the XML
  parser reject the update list.
- After cancel, send SIGTERM and wait ten seconds before SIGKILL, so
  transactional-update can discard the snapshot.
- Do not restart packagekitd from %post while TRANSACTIONAL_UPDATE
  is set. That restart hits the daemon which is running the update.
- Show an ERROR: line from snapper or the snapshot tools. Exit 4
  without a dependency sentence is a transaction error.
- Release 10. The repository already has 0.1.0-9.1.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 01:02:33 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- When the package transaction fails, show the conflict. zypper writes
  that on stderr. The stdout tail was the download cache, "exit status
  8", and "Discarding snapshot".
- Say, in plain language, when two packages own one file or a dependency
  cannot be satisfied. transactional-update exits 1 for every zypper
  failure, so the real code is taken from "failed with exit code".
  A failure that gives no reason still says nothing was changed.
- Keep the two command streams apart until the command exits, then
  append stderr. A progress line no longer lands in the middle of a
  conflict line.
- Release 9.

-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Nov 03 00:33:19 UTC 2026 - ahjolinna <ahjolinna@yahoo.com>

- When a repository file returns HTTP 404, name the missing packages.
  Discover keeps the tail of a long error, which was the snapshot
  cleanup, so a rebuild in progress looked like a silent failure.
- Release 8. The repository already has 0.1.0-7.1.

